From 097b54f5e25499aff88692fac3fa916274427c88 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 03:50:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): a capture gap can no longer fork a claim's run;
 complete --force closes a parked card [daveey] (#409)

* fix(kanban): a capture gap can no longer fork a claim's run; complete --force closes a parked card [daveey]

Live (hub, 2026-10-30 23:43): a probe with a temp HERMES_HOME that inherited a worker's HERMES_KANBAN_DB
opened the live board, read sync as off from its empty home and dropped every capture trigger for ~50 s.
A claim in that gap left the lease's run uid in kanban_sync_state.pending_run_uid; the run row got another
uid, the Board's echo made a second (pending_sync) run row with the lease uid (one dispatch, two runs, the
first orphaned `running`), and the next local run insert on any card -- a manual `kanban complete` -- took the
stale pending uid: UNIQUE constraint failed: task_runs.uid.

- install_or_remove keeps the triggers of a board attached to the Board service unless that home's config
  explicitly turns sync off (enabled: false, or a boards list without it); it logs instead.
- claim_and_open_run writes the lease's run uid into the run row itself (no pending hand-off through the
  insert trigger), clears any stale pending uid, and adopts a pending_sync placeholder of that uid when the
  Board's echo was pulled before the claim txn.
- complete_task(force=True) also closes a `scheduled` card, so `hermes kanban complete --force` finishes a
  parked placement-forwarded card and archives its placed copy (#371's path) without an unblock race.

* fix(kanban): workflow allows scheduled -> done, matching force-complete of a parked card [daveey]
